      "evidence": [
        {
          "id": "S14E7",
          "sourceId": "da2cb17df8cb821c",
          "quote": "It’s tempting to describe a model to deploy in a coding agent, walk away, and come back to a working endpoint."
        },
        {
          "id": "S14E8",
          "sourceId": "da2cb17df8cb821c",
          "quote": "In practice, an unguided coding agent might make wrong decisions, producing endpoints that are fragile, costly, or quietly wrong."
        },
        {
          "id": "S14E9",
          "sourceId": "da2cb17df8cb821c",
          "quote": "The problem gets worse for newer models, since their training data might not include the latest deployment knowledge."
        },
        {
          "id": "S14E11",
          "sourceId": "da2cb17df8cb821c",
          "quote": "You install six skills from Hugging Face Skills , point a coding agent at a Hugging Face model, and get back a real-time endpoint with"
        },
        {
          "id": "S14E12",
          "sourceId": "da2cb17df8cb821c",
          "quote": "autoscaling, Amazon CloudWatch alarms, the correct serving container from the AWS Deep Learning Containers (DLC) catalog, and a verified teardown path."
        },
        {
          "id": "S9E1",
          "sourceId": "0e6a0fab439f9601",
          "quote": "Asteroids, sometimes called minor planets, are rocky, airless remnants left over from the early formation of our solar system about 4.6 billion years ago."
        },
        {
          "id": "S9E2",
          "sourceId": "0e6a0fab439f9601",
          "quote": "Most asteroids can be found orbiting the Sun between Mars and Jupiter within the main asteroid belt."
        },
        {
          "id": "S9E3",
          "sourceId": "0e6a0fab439f9601",
          "quote": "Asteroids range in size from Vesta – the largest at about 329 miles (530 kilometers) in diameter – to bodies that are less than 33"
        },
        {
          "id": "S9E5",
          "sourceId": "0e6a0fab439f9601",
          "quote": "The total mass of all the asteroids combined is less than that of Earth's Moon."
        },
        {
          "id": "S9E4",
          "sourceId": "0e6a0fab439f9601",
          "quote": "feet (10 meters) across."
        },
        {
          "id": "S16E2",
          "sourceId": "345db337312aaeeb",
          "quote": "In other words, as masculine as you can get. That’s the image, yet women have mined around the world throughout history."
        },
        {
          "id": "S16E5",
          "sourceId": "345db337312aaeeb",
          "quote": "Early modern mining was a household affair, with all members of the family performing mining tasks."
        },
        {
          "id": "S16E11",
          "sourceId": "345db337312aaeeb",
          "quote": "Over a span of two centuries, women were evicted from the mines of Europe and North America as “protective” laws banned them from mining."
        },
        {
          "id": "S16E7",
          "sourceId": "345db337312aaeeb",
          "quote": "But because mining has been considered and even legislated as men’s work, Romano and Papastefanaki argue that women have largely been erased from the"
        },
        {
          "id": "S16E8",
          "sourceId": "345db337312aaeeb",
          "quote": "history of mining."
        },
        {
          "id": "S12E1",
          "sourceId": "fb5fae89f13eddf0",
          "quote": "GDPNow as of today is 5.1% q/q AR for Q3: Figure 1: GDP (black), August Survey of Professional Forecasters (purple), GDPNow (light blue square), Goldman"
        },
        {
          "id": "S12E4",
          "sourceId": "fb5fae89f13eddf0",
          "quote": "GDPNow is well above other nowcasts, with consumption nowcasted to grow 4.1%, and – perhaps more importantly – “core GDP” 4.7% q/q AR."
        },
        {
          "id": "S12E5",
          "sourceId": "fb5fae89f13eddf0",
          "quote": "Interestingly, the just released FT-Booth forecast , for 2% q4/q4 growth, is more in line with the August SPF, and with the NY Fed nowcast"
        }
